## Session 19 — major progress; criterion NOT met (marker not written)

**Core discovery:** Ran the **full 8/tcp suite for the first time** (prior sessions only validated dir_reuse standalone) → 13/17 PASS, revealing the real blocker is the **mht tradeoff**: tcp_dlm_scaling needs low mht (PASS 8/8 @ mht=50), dir_reuse needs high mht — both stress the same shared dir-EX lock, so one global knob can't satisfy both. Resolution requires making dir_reuse correct at low mht.

**Validated KEEP fix:** inode-cluster cached-allocated skip (the inverse of the sess38 cached-FREE ENOENT bug) — cut inode FUA reads ~30%, **proven safe** (cache_coherency/zero_silent_loss/strong_consistency/crash_consistency all 8/8).

**Path to resolving the tradeoff, narrowed via RULE-4 experiments:**
- `dir_release_invalidate=1` cuts dir_reuse mht=50 loss **18 → ~2** failrounds (handoff-gated release-side).
- `dir_coherent_modify=1` (acquire-side content-compare) makes it **fully correct** (failrounds=0) but ~5× too slow (per-addname).
- **Refuted** (all worse/slower): force_coherent, dir_release_fua_write, trylock-retry+MXFS_IF_DIR_RELOAD. Lesson: aggressive/ungated reload clobbers; the fix must be handoff-gated AND surgical.

**Ended mid-implementation of the most promising fix** (build `F141D09D`, builds clean, **untested**): made `dir_coherent_modify`'s scan **handoff-gated** via a new `i_dlm_dir_coherent_gen` field — runs once per handoff instead of per addname, aiming to keep its correctness while fixing the 5× slowness.

**Next session's first action** (recorded in `sess19run-UNTESTED-handoff-gated-coherent-modify-build-F141D09D`): deploy F141D09D, test `mht=50 + dir_release_invalidate=1 + dir_coherent_modify=1` — if correct AND <300s, set those as defaults and re-validate the full 1/2/4/8 tcp suites. Six `sess19run-*` ccmemory entries + xfs/pal awareness docs capture everything.

